@startuml Cross-Domain Semantic Bridges

package "Smart City Ontology" {
    ' | Stereotype | Meaning |
    ' |---|---|
    ' | `<<key>>` | Entities that are **directly read or compared** during the coordination decision — the agent must retrieve and reason about their properties to assign an EV to a charging slot |
    ' | `<<bridge>>` | The **cross-domain gap marker** — an entity that exists in one ontology but whose counterpart lives in the other; the semantic mapping the agent must negotiate |
    ' | `<<context>>` | Entities that provide **structural topology** — necessary to traverse the graph and locate the key entities, but not themselves decision variables |
    ' | `<<abstract>>` | **Base classes** from the CIM hierarchy — present only to satisfy inheritance chains; carry no scenario-specific semantics |
    ' | `<<open-reference>>` | An entity **referenced by this ontology but defined in another** — an incomplete cross-domain slot the agent must resolve through reasoning rather than graph traversal |

    <style>
    ClassDiagram {
        .key {
            BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
            LineColor       #FFC107
            FontStyle       bold
        }
        .context {
            BackgroundColor #D6EAF8
            LineColor       #2E86C1
        }
        .abstract {
            BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
            LineColor       #AAAAAA
            FontColor       #888888
        }
        .bridge {
            BackgroundColor #FDDDE6
            LineColor       #E91E63
            FontStyle       bold
        }
        .abstract {
            BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
            LineColor       #AAAAAA
            FontColor       #888888
        }
        .open-reference {
            BackgroundColor #FFE0B2
            LineColor       #E65100
            FontStyle       italic
        }
    }
    </style>

    ' ----- smart-city-object.puml > smart-city-ev.puml > smart-city-crossdomain.puml > smart-city-topology.puml -----

    enum GeoType {
        Point
        LineString
        Polygon
        MultiPoint
        MultiLineString
        MultiPolygon
    }

    ' <<bridge>> decision:
    ' - **`GeoLocation`** — the Smart City side of the GeoLocation ↔ Location semantic gap. Uses GeoJSON-typed geometry
    '   (type: GeoType, coordinates: string) as opposed to the Energy Grid CIM scalar Cartesian model
    '   (xPosition/yPosition). The agent must negotiate this coordinate system mismatch when correlating
    '   Smart City geographic entities with grid asset zones (e.g., SubGeographicalRegion → Substation).
    entity GeoLocation <<bridge>> {
        type: GeoType
        coordinates: string /' Depends on the type of the location. '/
    }

    ' Spatial-object represents everything that can have a spatial representation.
    ' It is superclass of feature and geometry.
    ' GeoSPARQL 1.0 is an OGC Standard.Copyright (c) 2012 Open Geospatial Consortium.
    entity SpatialObject <<abstract>> {
    }

    ' The class represents the top-level geometry type.
    ' This class is equivalent to the UML class GM_Object defined in ISO 19107, and it is superclass of all geometry types.
    ' GeoSPARQL 1.0 is an OGC Standard.Copyright (c) 2012 Open Geospatial Consortium.
    entity Geometry <<abstract>> extends SpatialObject {
    }

    ' This class represents the top-level feature type.
    ' This class is equivalent to GFI_Feature defined in ISO 19156:2011, and it is superclass of all feature types.
    ' GeoSPARQL 1.0 is an OGC Standard.Copyright (c) 2012 Open Geospatial Consortium.
    entity Feature <<abstract>> extends SpatialObject {
    }

    SpatialObject --> SpatialObject : Contains

    SpatialObject --> SpatialObject : Within

    Feature --> Geometry : hasGeometry

