    ' ----- energy-grid-electric-vehicle.puml -----

    ' NOTE: The modeling of ElectricVehicle is incomplete inside the Energy Grid ontology:
    ' - ElectricVehicle lives under Ontology/Prosumers/ in the energy grid ontology
    ' - Authors modeled it as a consumer/producer of energy
    ' - Has a dangling relationship with EVChargingStation (From Smart City ontology)
    ' - No relationship to energy grid entities like UsagePoint, CustomerLoad, EquivalentLoad, etc.

    ' NOTE: EVChargingStation is referenced here for cross-domain linkage,
    ' but it is not defined in the Energy Grid ontology. It belongs to the Smart City ontology.
    entity EVChargingStation <<open-reference>> {
    }

    ' Adapted from CIM and https://github.com/smart-data-models/dataModel.EnergyCIM/ data models: an electric vehicle model
    ' An electric vehicle (EV) is a vehicle that uses one or more electric motors or traction motors for propulsion.
    ' An electric vehicle may be powered through a collector system by electricity from off-vehicle sources,
    ' or may be self-contained with a battery, solar panels, fuel cells or an electric generator to convert fuel to electricity.
    '
    ' <<key>> decision:
    ' - **`ElectricVehicle`** — the demand side of the problem. Its `chargeRateMax` sets the upper bound on which station power levels are compatible, `chargeTarget` quantifies how much energy is needed, and `chargeTargetTimestamp` establishes urgency. Without these, no assignment decision can be made.
    entity ElectricVehicle <<key>> {
            evName: string /' The name of the electric vehicle. '/
            ' capacity: double /' Total EV battery capacity. '/
            ' chargeMin: double /' Minimum charge limit. '/
            ' chargeRateMin: double /' Minimum charging rate. '/
            chargeRateMax: double /' Maximum charging rate. '/
            ' dischargeRateMin: double /' Minimum discharge rate. '/
            ' dischargeRateMax: double /' Maximum discharge rate. '/
            ' chargeTarget: double /' Target capacity to be charged '/
            ' chargeTargetTimestamp: dateTime /' Target end datetime to be charged '/
            ' -- connectedTo_ChargingStation --> EVChargingStation /' EV --> ChargingStation '/
    }

    ElectricVehicle --> EVChargingStation : connectedTo_ChargingStation /' EV --> ChargingStation '/

    note right of EVChargingStation
    Not defined in Energy Grid;
    belongs to Smart City ontology.
    end note

    ' ----- energy-grid-customer-load.puml (energy-grid-substation.puml already inlined above) -----

        ' A connection of energy generation or consumption on the power system model.
        entity EnergyConnection <<abstract>> extends ConductingEquipment {
        }

        ' According to IEC 61970-301, an EnergyConsumer is a generic user of energy - a  point of consumption on the power system model.
        ' EnergyConsumer.pfixed, .qfixed, .pfixedPct and .qfixedPct have meaning
        ' only if there is no LoadResponseCharacteristic associated with EnergyConsumer or
        ' if LoadResponseCharacteristic.exponentModel is set to False.
        entity EnergyConsumer <<context>> extends EnergyConnection {
            ' pfixed: float /' Active power of the load that is a fixed quantity and does not vary as load group value varies. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node.  '/
            ' pfixedPct: float /' Fixed active power as a percentage of load group fixed active power. Used to represent the time-varying components.  Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. '/
            ' qfixed: float /' Reactive power of the load that is a fixed quantity and does not vary as load group value varies. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. '/
            ' qfixedPct: float /' Fixed reactive power as a percentage of load group fixed reactive power. Used to represent the time-varying components.  Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. '/
        }

        ' According to IEC 61968-13, a MV  customer is a CustomerLoad.
        '
        ' <<key>> decision:
        ' - **`CustomerLoad`** — MV background load contributing to transformer stress. Its `p` (active power) is part of the total load
        '   the transformer must carry before any EV charging is added. The agent must sum all CustomerLoad.p values under a
        '   transformer to correctly compute available headroom: headroom = ratedS − (ΣCustomerLoad.p + ΣEquivalentLoad.p + ΣUsagePoint.estimatedLoad).
        '   Without it, the agent risks overloading a transformer that is already near capacity from MV commercial/industrial customers.
        entity CustomerLoad <<key>> extends EnergyConsumer {
            p: float /' Active power of the load. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. For voltage dependent loads the value is at rated voltage. Starting value for a steady state solution. Default: 0.0 '/
            ' q: float /' Reactive power of the load. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. For voltage dependent loads the value is at rated voltage. Starting value for a steady state solution. Default: 0.0 '/
            ' powerFactor: float /' the power factor value '/
        }

        ' According to IEC 61968-13, a LV customer is an EquivalentLoad.
        ' An EquivalentLoad has the attribute customerCount having its value greater than one
        ' to indicate the number of customers attached.
        ' The voltage level is specified by a voltage level that contains this EquivalentLoad.
        entity EquivalentLoad <<key>> extends EnergyConsumer {
            p: float /' Active power of the load. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. For voltage dependent loads the value is at rated voltage. Starting value for a steady state solution. Default: 0.0 '/
            ' q: float /' Reactive power of the load. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. For voltage dependent loads the value is at rated voltage. Starting value for a steady state solution. Default: 0.0 '/
            ' powerFactor: float /' the power factor value '/
            customerCount: integer /' the attribute that indicate the number of customers attached '/    
        }

}

' ===== Cross-Domain Semantic Bridges =====

"Energy Grid Ontology.EVChargingStation" ..> "Smart City Ontology.EVChargingStation" : resolves_to\n(defined in SC, not EG)
"Smart City Ontology.EVChargingStation" .. "Energy Grid Ontology.CustomerLoad" : same physical location\n(SC asset <-> EG load entity)
"Smart City Ontology.District" ..> "Energy Grid Ontology.SubGeographicalRegion" : civic zone\nvs.\nelectrical topology zone
"Smart City Ontology.Neighbourhood" ..> "Energy Grid Ontology.Substation" : neighbourhood\nvs.\nsubstation service area
"Smart City Ontology.GeoLocation" ..> "Energy Grid Ontology.Location" : GeoJSON geometry\nvs.\nCIM Cartesian (x, y)


@enduml
